    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Alcohol use disorder, severe; heavy daily drinking for most of his adult life; synthetic modern episode linked to his documented heavy drinking</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F10.20</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of DSM-5-TR severe alcohol use disorder (seven criteria); person-first language; not a claim about his real diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Raised transferrin saturation and ferritin found on routine intake tests, cause not yet known (heavy drinking, liver disease or iron overload)</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R79.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding; superseded when HFE testing gave the diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hereditary hemochromatosis, HFE C282Y homozygous, with iron overload (ferritin over 1,000 ng/mL) and no advanced liver fibrosis on imaging</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E83.110</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis. Whether he had hemochromatosis is disputed (CLM-0013); the modern diagnosis is not offered as proof of it.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate; Mood Disorder Questionnaire negative and no history of mania or hypomania</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F32.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; not a claim about his real mood. The roster&apos;s bipolar disorder lead is disputed (CLM-0014) and is not used.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Essential hypertension, stage 2, with heavy drinking contributing</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I10</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis confirmed by home readings.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Post-concussion symptoms (headaches, slowed thinking and forgetfulness) after repeated head injuries, most recently a concussion with a skull fracture a year ago; chronic traumatic encephalopathy is not diagnosed</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F07.81</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented head injuries; alcohol and depression also affect the symptoms.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Prediabetes (HbA1c 6.1%)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R73.03</td><td>S — Synthetic finding on diabetes screening; iron overload and alcohol both raise the risk of diabetes.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

